From ae06a62e7530ee90218ab8f63933f46ea4785031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:11:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: Drain deferred GPUVM BOs when a kernel mapping is
 dropped

KernelMappingInner holds a GpuVmBo reference, which is released with
drm_gpuvm_bo_put_deferred(): the last put only moves the vm_bo to the
GPUVM's deferred list, and the vm_bo, its GEM reference and its pages
are freed only when someone calls drm_gpuvm_bo_deferred_cleanup() on
that GPUVM. User VMs do that when they are torn down, but kernel
mappings live in the device's kernel VM, which is never torn down. So
every BO that was ever mapped into the kernel VM stays allocated after
its last user is gone. Userspace timestamp buffers are mapped there:
each process that loads a model with llama.cpp's Vulkan backend left
about 239 MB of unevictable shmem behind after a clean exit, with no
GPU faults, and 3.8 GB had accumulated on one machine.

Drop the GpuVmBo explicitly and drain the owner's deferred list when a
KernelMappingInner is dropped. Field order is unchanged, so the GEM
reference and then the owning GPUVM are released after the cleanup, as
the comment on the struct requires. KernelMapping::drop releases its
exec lock before the mapping's node (and with it this data) is dropped.

This is the KernelMappingInner part of upstream asahi-wip commit
256b1204c12d ("drm/asahi: Adjustment for v7.2 + partial drm-rust v7.3",
Janne Grunau), which also reorders the fields; the asahi-wip commit this
kernel is based on (e09c62843a8e) predates it. Not needed from 7.3.1
(c2e6784b008c has it).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/mmu.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/mmu.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/mmu.rs
index b09509832..9291f43eb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/mmu.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/mmu.rs
@@ -631,6 +631,13 @@ pub(crate) struct KernelMappingInner {
     mapped_size: usize,
 }
 
+impl Drop for KernelMappingInner {
+    fn drop(&mut self) {
+        self.bo = None;
+        self.owner.deferred_cleanup();
+    }
+}
+
 /// An object mapping into a [`Vm`], which reserves the address range from use by other mappings.
 pub(crate) struct KernelMapping(mm::Node<(), KernelMappingInner>);
 
-- 
2.56.0

